{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RZ2uMnRG5ZisKFja6K8TvB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Gandalf Runtime Host (Tier-1) — Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n2\t\n3\t> test-command: `node --test test/*.test.mjs`\n4\t> Reuse the shipped `seam/*.mjs` + `test/harness.mjs`; additive only (`runtime/` + `test/runtime-*` + docs).\n5\t> Single-family (`cross_model:false`). Every wave holds or grows the test count; the existing 130 canary\n6\t> tests must stay green every wave.\n7\t\n8\t## Wave 1 — the deterministic seam-pass composer (`runtime/seam-pass.mjs`)\n9\t**Goal:** a pure `applySeamPass(rawDraft, { cross_model = false }) -> conformantOutput` that turns a model's\n10\tRAW draft into a canary-conformant graded advisor output, reusing the shipped seams.\n11\t\n12\t**Changes:**\n13\t- `runtime/seam-pass.mjs` exporting `applySeamPass`. Behavior:\n14\t  - Validate the raw draft shape (object with `reasoning`, `verdict`, arrays `findings`/`nitpicks`/\n15\t    `elevations`); on a malformed draft throw a NAMED error (`SeamPassInputError`) — never fabricate.\n16\t  - **findings** — by `kind`: `diagnose` → `stampDiagnoseCoreProvenance`; `anticipate` →\n17\t    `composeAnticipation` (ensure `future_state_condition` + `enabling_assumption` + `subject_cardinality:1`);\n18\t    `situate` → `composeSituate`. Drop any finding with rung `REFUTED` (`dropsFromOutput`).\n19\t  - **elevations** — `vetElevationRefutation` (Tier-1: no independent refuter ran → every elevation is\n20\t    downgraded to SPECULATIVE + the `NO_INDEPENDENT_REFUTATION_STAMP`), then set `tier` from\n21\t    `labelTier(elevation, { cross_model })` (capped PROMISING; SPECULATIVE here). Drop REFUTED.\n22\t  - **risk_labels** — `composeRiskLabels(output)` (present legs only, envelope rung, PROMISING ceiling).\n23\t  - Assemble `{ schema_version, cross_model:false, degraded, reasoning (BEFORE verdict), verdict, findings,\n24\t    nitpicks, elevations, risk_labels }`; if any item ran `degraded:true`, set top-level `degraded:true` (B6).\n25\t- `test/runtime-seam-pass.test.mjs` (+ a raw-draft fixture).\n26\t\n27\t**Done-when (`node --test test/runtime-seam-pass.test.mjs` green AND the full `node --test test/*.test.mjs`\n28\tstill 130+ green):**\n29\t- Given a raw draft with diagnose + situate + anticipate findings and ≥2 elevations, When `applySeamPass`,\n30\t  Then `assertIncrement1Conformant(out)` PASSES.\n31\t- Every output elevation has `tier === 'SPECULATIVE'` AND carries the no-independent-refutation stamp.\n32\t- Each `diagnose` finding carries the `gandalf_core` provenance; each `anticipate` finding has a populated\n33\t  `future_state_condition` + `enabling_assumption` + `subject_cardinality === 1`.\n34\t- A finding/elevation with rung `REFUTED` is ABSENT from the output (only-REFUTED-drops).\n35\t- `risk_labels` has exactly one entry per present leg, each `tier === 'PROMISING'` (single-family).\n36\t- A per-item `degraded:true` forces top-level `degraded:true` (no silent degradation).\n37\t- A malformed raw draft (missing `findings`, or a non-object) throws `SeamPassInputError`; no partial output.\n38\t\n39\t## Wave 2 — the thin runtime entry CLI (`runtime/gandalf-run.mjs`) + the raw-draft contract\n40\t**Goal:** the runnable host — read a raw draft, seam-pass it, validate, emit the conformant output; the\n41\tdocumented contract for what the model must emit.\n42\t\n43\t**Changes:**\n44\t- `runtime/gandalf-run.mjs` (a real entrypoint: `process.argv` flags `--input <file>` | stdin, `--output\n45\t  <file>` | stdout): read raw draft JSON → `applySeamPass` → `assertIncrement1Conformant` → write the\n46\t  conformant JSON. On malformed input or a failed assertion: exit non-zero with an honest stderr message and\n47\t  write NOTHING (no partial/forged output).\n48\t- `runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md` — documents the raw draft the model emits in runtime mode (the schema\n49\t  fields per item; \"emit ONLY this JSON object as the final message; do NOT self-assign tiers/stamps — the\n50\t  host applies them\").\n51\t- `test/runtime-entry.test.mjs` — spawn `node runtime/gandalf-run.mjs` (child process) over a fixture via\n52\t  both `--input` and stdin; assert the written output re-loads + `assertIncrement1Conformant` passes; assert\n53\t  malformed input → non-zero exit + stderr + no output file.\n54\t\n55\t**Done-when (`node --test test/*.test.mjs` green, 130 + Wave-1 + Wave-2):**\n56\t- `node runtime/gandalf-run.mjs --input <fixture> --output <tmp>` exits 0 and `<tmp>` re-loads to a\n57\t  conformant output (`assertIncrement1Conformant` passes).\n58\t- The stdin path produces byte-identical output to the `--input` path for the same fixture.\n59\t- Malformed input → non-zero exit, an honest stderr reason, and NO output file written.\n60\t- `RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md` exists and names every per-item field the seam pass consumes.\n61\t\n62\t## Wave 3 — integration + docs (PROJECT DONE)\n63\t**Goal:** prove the end-to-end host, and update the skill's own docs so the host is no longer \"aspirational.\"\n64\t**Changes:**\n65\t- `test/runtime-integration.test.mjs` — a representative raw draft → `gandalf-run.mjs` → conformant output;\n66\t  assert the candid diagnosis survives, elevations are SPECULATIVE-stamped, risk_labels PROMISING-capped.\n67\t- `SKILL.md` §RUNTIME — replace the \"intended host (see LESSONS.md)\" aspiration with a pointer to the real\n68\t  `runtime/gandalf-run.mjs` (model emits the raw draft per `runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md`; the host applies\n69\t  the seams). LESSONS.md + a `journal/000N-runtime-host.md` entry record the host landed (Tier-1; live\n70\t  refuters still a follow-on).\n71\t**Done-when:** `node --test test/*.test.mjs` green (130 + all runtime tests); SKILL.md §RUNTIME points at the\n72\treal host; the journal/LESSONS note the Tier-1 host shipped and that live-refuter PROMISING is the follow-on.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5be1dd9-902a-4dd8-b322-fde72478c37a","uuid":"65c47fd2-f02c-450d-abb0-7147d2e06a43","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:22:01.983Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\skills\\gandalf\\planning\\runtime-host\\IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md","content":"# Gandalf Runtime Host (Tier-1) — Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n\n> test-command: `node --test test/*.test.mjs`\n> Reuse the shipped `seam/*.mjs` + `test/harness.mjs`; additive only (`runtime/` + `test/runtime-*` + docs).\n> Single-family (`cross_model:false`). Every wave holds or grows the test count; the existing 130 canary\n> tests must stay green every wave.\n\n## Wave 1 — the deterministic seam-pass composer (`runtime/seam-pass.mjs`)\n**Goal:** a pure `applySeamPass(rawDraft, { cross_model = false }) -> conformantOutput` that turns a model's\nRAW draft into a canary-conformant graded advisor output, reusing the shipped seams.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `runtime/seam-pass.mjs` exporting `applySeamPass`. Behavior:\n  - Validate the raw draft shape (object with `reasoning`, `verdict`, arrays `findings`/`nitpicks`/\n    `elevations`); on a malformed draft throw a NAMED error (`SeamPassInputError`) — never fabricate.\n  - **findings** — by `kind`: `diagnose` → `stampDiagnoseCoreProvenance`; `anticipate` →\n    `composeAnticipation` (ensure `future_state_condition` + `enabling_assumption` + `subject_cardinality:1`);\n    `situate` → `composeSituate`. Drop any finding with rung `REFUTED` (`dropsFromOutput`).\n  - **elevations** — `vetElevationRefutation` (Tier-1: no independent refuter ran → every elevation is\n    downgraded to SPECULATIVE + the `NO_INDEPENDENT_REFUTATION_STAMP`), then set `tier` from\n    `labelTier(elevation, { cross_model })` (capped PROMISING; SPECULATIVE here). Drop REFUTED.\n  - **risk_labels** — `composeRiskLabels(output)` (present legs only, envelope rung, PROMISING ceiling).\n  - Assemble `{ schema_version, cross_model:false, degraded, reasoning (BEFORE verdict), verdict, findings,\n    nitpicks, elevations, risk_labels }`; if any item ran `degraded:true`, set top-level `degraded:true` (B6).\n- `test/runtime-seam-pass.test.mjs` (+ a raw-draft fixture).\n\n**Done-when (`node --test test/runtime-seam-pass.test.mjs` green AND the full `node --test test/*.test.mjs`\nstill 130+ green):**\n- Given a raw draft with diagnose + situate + anticipate findings and ≥2 elevations, When `applySeamPass`,\n  Then `assertIncrement1Conformant(out)` PASSES.\n- Every output elevation has `tier === 'SPECULATIVE'` AND carries the no-independent-refutation stamp.\n- Each `diagnose` finding carries the `gandalf_core` provenance; each `anticipate` finding has a populated\n  `future_state_condition` + `enabling_assumption` + `subject_cardinality === 1`.\n- A finding/elevation with rung `REFUTED` is ABSENT from the output (only-REFUTED-drops).\n- `risk_labels` has exactly one entry per present leg, each `tier === 'PROMISING'` (single-family).\n- A per-item `degraded:true` forces top-level `degraded:true` (no silent degradation).\n- A malformed raw draft (missing `findings`, or a non-object) throws `SeamPassInputError`; no partial output.\n\n## Wave 2 — the thin runtime entry CLI (`runtime/gandalf-run.mjs`) + the raw-draft contract\n**Goal:** the runnable host — read a raw draft, seam-pass it, validate, emit the conformant output; the\ndocumented contract for what the model must emit.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `runtime/gandalf-run.mjs` (a real entrypoint: `process.argv` flags `--input <file>` | stdin, `--output\n  <file>` | stdout): read raw draft JSON → `applySeamPass` → `assertIncrement1Conformant` → write the\n  conformant JSON. On malformed input or a failed assertion: exit non-zero with an honest stderr message and\n  write NOTHING (no partial/forged output).\n- `runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md` — documents the raw draft the model emits in runtime mode (the schema\n  fields per item; \"emit ONLY this JSON object as the final message; do NOT self-assign tiers/stamps — the\n  host applies them\").\n- `test/runtime-entry.test.mjs` — spawn `node runtime/gandalf-run.mjs` (child process) over a fixture via\n  both `--input` and stdin; assert the written output re-loads + `assertIncrement1Conformant` passes; assert\n  malformed input → non-zero exit + stderr + no output file.\n\n**Done-when (`node --test test/*.test.mjs` green, 130 + Wave-1 + Wave-2):**\n- `node runtime/gandalf-run.mjs --input <fixture> --output <tmp>` exits 0 and `<tmp>` re-loads to a\n  conformant output (`assertIncrement1Conformant` passes).\n- The stdin path produces byte-identical output to the `--input` path for the same fixture.\n- Malformed input → non-zero exit, an honest stderr reason, and NO output file written.\n- `RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md` exists and names every per-item field the seam pass consumes.\n\n## Wave 3 — integration + docs (PROJECT DONE)\n**Goal:** prove the end-to-end host, and update the skill's own docs so the host is no longer \"aspirational.\"\n**Changes:**\n- `test/runtime-integration.test.mjs` — a representative raw draft → `gandalf-run.mjs` → conformant output;\n  assert the candid diagnosis survives, elevations are SPECULATIVE-stamped, risk_labels PROMISING-capped.\n- `SKILL.md` §RUNTIME — replace the \"intended host (see LESSONS.md)\" aspiration with a pointer to the real\n  `runtime/gandalf-run.mjs` (model emits the raw draft per `runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md`; the host applies\n  the seams). LESSONS.md + a `journal/000N-runtime-host.md` entry record the host landed (Tier-1; live\n  refuters still a follow-on).\n**Done-when:** `node --test test/*.test.mjs` green (130 + all runtime tests); SKILL.md §RUNTIME points at the\nreal host; the journal/LESSONS note the Tier-1 host shipped and that live-refuter PROMISING is the follow-on.\n","numLines":73,"startLine":1,"totalLines":73}}}
