{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01RE14q9j5ZckC6QdZFGiC7w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Planning Trio Session Summary — `runtime-host`\n\n**Member document:** Gandalf Runtime Host (Tier-1) — Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready) (`skills/gandalf/planning/runtime-host/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`, with intake context from the sibling `DESCRIPTION.md`)\n\n### What the session decided to build\n- **The build target is the \"missing runtime host\"** for the already-shipped Gandalf v1 skill — the \"thin runtime entry\" that prior build logs (`crucible-advisor/EXECUTION-LOG.md`, `LESSONS.md`, `journal/0001`) flagged as an open follow-up.\n- **Its job is to convert a model's RAW draft into a canary-conformant output** — taking un-stamped findings/elevations/diagnosis and running them through the shipped deterministic seam engine (`seam/*.mjs`) to emit an honestly-graded advisor output validated by the shipped `assertIncrement1Conformant`.\n- **Motivation is grounded in an observed failure:** the authors' first real run showed the model \"keeps hand-approximating tier stamps and failing the canary\" — the host makes grades deterministic instead of model-self-asserted.\n\n### Scope boundary (Tier-1, by design)\n- **Tier-1 = deterministic seam pass over ONE model run.** It explicitly does NOT dispatch live independent named-defeater refuters or the researchPrime SITUATE commission (those need the `agent()` seam that `seam/refute.mjs:26-28` flags as the unrun integration point).\n- **Consequent honest grading floor:** every elevation lands at **SPECULATIVE** carrying `NO_INDEPENDENT_REFUTATION_STAMP`; diagnosis findings keep evidence rungs + `gandalf_core` provenance; `risk_labels` cap at single-family **PROMISING** ceiling; only **REFUTED** items drop.\n- **Live-refuter PROMISING tier is a sequenced follow-on, not in this effort.**\n\n### Engineering constraints locked in\n- **Reuse, never fork:** the host adds glue + a CLI entry only, reusing named exports from `refute.mjs`, `score-label.mjs`, `diagnose-core.mjs`, `anticipate.mjs`, `situate.mjs`, and `harness.mjs`. It invents no new grading logic.\n- **Additive only:** new `runtime/` dir + `test/runtime-*.test.mjs` + a docs touch to `SKILL.md §RUNTIME`/`LESSONS.md`/`journal/`; no unrelated repo files.\n- **Gate discipline (PRINCIPLE-D):** ground-truth gate is `node --test test/*.test.mjs`; the existing **130 canary tests must stay green every wave**; single-family `cross_model:false`; no npm deps (Node 20+).\n- **Honesty non-negotiable:** a malformed/partial raw draft → a NAMED error (`SeamPassInputError`), never a fabricated finding or forged output; per-item degradation forces top-level `degraded:true` (B6).\n\n### Three-wave Foreman-ready plan\n- **Wave 1 — deterministic seam-pass composer (`runtime/seam-pass.mjs`):** pure `applySeamPass(rawDraft, {cross_model=false})`; routes findings by `kind` (diagnose/anticipate/situate), vets+downgrades elevations to SPECULATIVE, composes risk labels, assembles output with `reasoning` before `verdict`. Done-when: new test green AND full suite still 130+.\n- **Wave 2 — thin CLI entry (`runtime/gandalf-run.mjs`) + raw-draft contract:** real entrypoint (`--input`/stdin → `--output`/stdout) that reads, seam-passes, asserts conformance, and writes nothing on failure; plus `RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md` documenting what the model must emit (\"do NOT self-assign tiers/stamps — the host applies them\"). Done-when includes stdin == `--input` byte-identical output.\n- **Wave 3 — integration + docs (PROJECT DONE):** end-to-end integration test; `SKILL.md §RUNTIME` updated from \"aspirational\" to point at the real host; LESSONS/journal record Tier-1 host shipped with live-refuter as the follow-on.\n\n### Outcome (per repo state, beyond the plan doc itself)\n- **The plan was executed and shipped:** commit `cd24857` lands the Tier-1 deterministic runtime host and the v1 bundle (`runtime/gandalf-run.mjs`, `runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md`, journal `0002-runtime-host.md`); follow-on commits `a1a48f6` (\"lenient input / strict output\") and `40584ca` (\"sanitize out-of-enum values\") refine input handling from live-smoke and 6-project-run lessons.\n\n---\n*Note: the session's anchors/North-Star header line was empty in the prompt, so the \"Anchors\" framing above is derived from the DESCRIPTION's non-negotiables rather than a separately stated anchor list.* Want me to also pull in the session's Crucible `MASTER-PLAN.md` for this runtime-host if you need the upstream framing/North-Star?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4545,"cache_read_input_tokens":40871,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4545},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5be1dd9-902a-4dd8-b322-fde72478c37a","uuid":"8978cb7e-e8e2-420b-8a92-b4bc4f402812","request_id":"req_011CcLjc4dBL17KeVtFDWLSG"}
